                     <provenance type="#m" cert="low"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_1">Exeter, Devon.
                        Cathedral church of St Peter</orgName><p>The corresponding Medieval
                        Libraries of Great Britain index card for this provenance records the
                        following evidence: <q>Formerly part of Lambeth Palace 104, fols. i, 1–
                        (Exeter) (see MS. Tanner 268). A note in Bishop Grandisson's hand on fol
                        170v.</q> However, this was questioned in MLGB3 (2010-2015): <q>MLGB2 states
                        that Lambeth Palace 188, fols. 168–174, was part of <ref
                        target="https://mlgb.bodleian.ox.ac.uk/catalog/book_2714">Lambeth Palace
                        104</ref>, fols. i, 1–208. But this is not obvious and nor does the supposed
                        hand of Grandisson resemble the bishop's normal hand (James
                        Willoughby).</q></p></provenance>
